From: sbe1v1k 25.12-6.18 port <noreply@sbe1v1k-build>
Subject: [PATCH] qca-nss-phy: map the legacy OUTPUT pin config to PIN_CONFIG_LEVEL

6.18 dropped PIN_CONFIG_OUTPUT from enum pin_config_param; driving a pin
to a level is expressed with PIN_CONFIG_LEVEL, whose argument is the
level itself.  nss_phy_linux_wrapper.h still aliases the vendor name to
the removed symbol, so qca8084_pinctrl.c fails to build:

  error: 'PIN_CONFIG_OUTPUT' undeclared

Point the alias at PIN_CONFIG_LEVEL.  The one consumer,
qca8084_gpio_pin_cfg_set(), already does exactly what LEVEL means: it
enables the output and drives nss_phy_pinconf_to_config_argument() onto
the pin.

Classification: portability (kernel API, no behaviour change).
--- a/nss_ext/nss_phy_linux_wrapper.h
+++ b/nss_ext/nss_phy_linux_wrapper.h
@@ -150,7 +150,7 @@
 #define NSS_PHY_PIN_CONFIG_DRIVE_STRENGTH	PIN_CONFIG_DRIVE_STRENGTH
 #define NSS_PHY_PIN_CONFIG_OUTPUT_ENABLE	PIN_CONFIG_OUTPUT_ENABLE
 #define NSS_PHY_PIN_CONFIG_INPUT_ENABLE	PIN_CONFIG_INPUT_ENABLE
-#define NSS_PHY_PIN_CONFIG_OUTPUT	PIN_CONFIG_OUTPUT
+#define NSS_PHY_PIN_CONFIG_OUTPUT	PIN_CONFIG_LEVEL
 
 #define nss_phy_pinconf_to_config_param	pinconf_to_config_param
 #define nss_phy_pinconf_to_config_argument	pinconf_to_config_argument
